Title of your proposed AI use case:
AI-Assisted Transfer of Licensor Process Data Sheets into Promec PDS

(Alternative: Automated Population of Promec PDS from Licensor Datasheets)

Which working step does the proposed AI use case address?
Preparation of process datasheets (PDS) for equipment and instruments, specifically the step 
where process data from the licensor’s Process Design Package (for example, licensor PDS for 
vessels, columns, heat exchangers, pumps, and compressors) is transferred into the company’s Promec PDS format. 
This takes place mainly during the Basic Engineering / FEED phase. It also applies whenever revised licensor datasheets 
require updates to the Promec PDS.

Describe the proposed AI solution:

Current situation: Process engineers read each licensor PDS, which usually comes as a PDF in the licensor’s 
own layout, units, and terminology. They then manually enter the data field by field into the corresponding Promec PDS. 
This data includes operating and design conditions, fluid properties, flow rates, materials, nozzle data, and notes.

Pain point: The work is repetitive and time-consuming, especially on projects with a large number of datasheets. Licensor formats, 
units, and terminology differ from Promec, so engineers have to convert units and map fields. Manual transcription can introduce typing 
errors, missed values, or inconsistent units. When the licensor issues a new revision, the changes have to be found and re-entered by hand.

Proposed AI support: An AI tool would read the licensor PDS (including scanned or non-standard PDFs) and extract the relevant parameters. 
It would map them to the matching Promec PDS fields, apply unit conversions, and generate a pre-filled Promec PDS draft. The tool would 
flag fields that are missing, ambiguous, or could not be confidently mapped, and link each value back to its location in the source document 
for traceability. When a licensor revision is issued, the AI would compare it with the previous version and highlight only the changed values to update.

Role of the engineer: The responsible process engineer reviews and verifies the pre-filled draft and fills in flagged or missing items. 
The engineer also applies engineering judgement where licensor data needs interpretation, such as design margins or project-specific requirements, 
before the Promec PDS is issued.
